  "comment": "Rules of tools/spec/owners.ps1 (contract 'owners'). 'units' lists every unit with its directory name, selftest dx range and the paths it owns (R3, R12), 'unitFiles': true (W0b) for the per-unit files every W1 unit owns by its name (assets/data/*/<n>.json, assets/lang/*/<n>.json, assets/tags/**/*.d/<n>.json, tools/import/overrides/<n>.json, tools/sounds/recipes/<n>.json), 'gfSubcommands' for its GloamingForest-only /twilightforest subcommands (literal paths without arguments; TF's own literals, read from TF's command classes, are partitioned by ids.subcommand), and under its own 'ids' the ids outside TF's namespace it creates ({kind: [full id or {id, mode: gen|manual}]}; gen by default; no other owner may have them; kind 'lang' takes translation keys that are not TF's en_us keys, e.g. the vanilla UI strings a unit defines in assets/lang/<locale>/<u>.json); 'ids' partitions every TF id per kind with ordered [glob, owner] rules (first match wins; globs match the id path without the namespace; '{a,b}' alternation, '*' any text); 'tagRegistryGroups' lists the directories of data/<ns>/tags/ that hold two-segment tag registries (tags/worldgen/biome/ is the tag registry 'worldgen/biome'; tags/twilight/ joins in one change with F1's import, see docs/spec/README.md); 'lang' maps en_us key patterns to an owner or to '$<kind>:<capture>' (the owner of that id). Ids no rule claims are reported (and listed under 'unclaimed' in docs/spec/README.md).",
